      "evidence_id": "e-db1d07fe91a6b1803852",
      "text": "In the heart of the Aegean Sea, Kimolos Island is one of Greece’s best-kept secrets. This tiny little island, part of the lovely Cycladic islands cluster, really is a haven for the type of traveller who craves a genuine, laid back experience. None of that fast-paced tourist nonsense here. Unlike some of its more well-known neighbours, Kimolos has a much more relaxed vibe. Stunning landscapes, quaint whitewashed houses with bright blue doors, narrow alleyways dressed in blooming bougainvillea, and soothing sounds of fishing boats bobbing up & down in the harbour.",
